# Uses that scripts/test_layout.mbtx accepts although its rules reject them.
# Each entry is `<file> <rule> # reason`, one line per use, so every new use
# needs its own decision. Rules: async-test, async-intrinsic, testing-import,
# wbtest-testing-import, clock.
http/src/rt/random.mbt clock # default_random is the host boundary for jitter and boundaries; callers take a random source with it as the default, so deterministic tests never read host entropy.
mttp/src/client/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The Driver executes NoLimiter's async boundary test while white-box access places its private sequence at Int64.MAX; issuing that many public admissions is infeasible, so black-box tests cannot verify refusal before sequence reuse.
mttp/src/client/ratelimit/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The Driver schedules cancellation and gate handoff while white-box tests count private holder/waiter references; successful later requests alone cannot prove these references were reclaimed.
mttp/src/client/ratelimit/moon.pkg wbtest-testing-import # The sim clocks advance virtual time while white-box tests measure private map sizes and sweep thresholds; public state() cannot reveal retained orphan entries, so black-box success alone cannot prove these resource bounds.
